# Material role binding focused checks

This runner records local source/model/kernel checks for the private eight-role
binding. It does not invoke a full original-owner fixture, ignored test, systemd
unit, product workload or server. Linux uses the existing Ubuntu toolchain/cache
without package, clock or service changes. Every lane refuses an existing output
directory and checks unchanged source/lock/qualification hashes before/after.
First failure/timeout is retained and stops the lane, never automatically retried.

From the repository root:

```powershell
python -B -m unittest discover -s tools/held-material-roles-074 -v
python -B tools/held-material-roles-074/check.py host
python -B tools/held-material-roles-074/check.py 194
python -B tools/held-material-roles-074/check.py 188
```

The first command is fully synthetic. Other commands run focused checks only,
with immutable receipts under target/held-material-roles-20261022. No timing or
allocation performance claim follows from compiler/test elapsed time. Mapping
is partial: worker and Armed root guardian descriptors, actual held executable
addressing and activation environment still need their own consuming joins.
